Two fixes to step 1 of process-email, which brings trunk work and the
mail outbox up to date before each pass. Each left a pass working
from the wrong state.

Patch 1: the trunk rebase picked up the mail outbox whenever the
list had moved since the outbox was built. That happened on this
pass. The fetch moved mail@upstream, and my two outbox commits and
the mail working copy were rebased onto trunk, so the mail workspace
checked out trunk. Running the old and new revsets at the operation
right after that fetch shows the difference. The old revset lists the
outbox commits and the mail working copy. The new one lists only
trunk work. I moved the outbox back by hand before going on.

Patch 2 is the fix I offered in "Re: need some way to close the loop
on threads" [1]. Once the whole outbox is merged, the bookmark has
nothing to rebase and stays on an old mail commit, which hides new
mail. I checked the new condition in a scratch repo with a missing
bookmark and with one behind the tip. jj bookmark set creates the
first and moves the second forward.

Both apply on trunk, and also with "[PATCH 0/3] Archive messages
that need no answer" [2] and "[PATCH 0/2] Reply to all on the list"
[3] in any order without conflict.

